pane-guard: '--not-a-declared-flag' is not a flag pane-guard declares. Declared: --help, --home, --instants-dir, --pane, --porcelain. Refused, not ignored: a parser that accepts what no spec declares is a second, hand-maintained copy of the flag list.
fleet pane-guard --pane <value>
    the send-keys contract: 0 safe / 10 queued / 11 mid-turn / 12 not-claude / 13 unknown
    --pane <value>               (required) the pane (session) name
    --home <value>               the record/pool store root; overrides $FLEET_HOME
    --instants-dir <value>       where instants live; overrides $FLEET_INSTANTS
    --porcelain                  machine form on stdout: tab-separated, no banner (NFR2-7)
    --help                       print this verb's derived usage and exit 0

exit codes:
    0  ok
    1  needs attention / check failed
    2  bad input
    3  no capacity
    4  refused by an admission rule
    pane-guard only (FD-10):
    0  safe
    10 queued-text
    11 mid-turn
    12 not-claude
    13 unknown-pane

